    "module": {
      "intro": "This module helps readers see that a learning problem does not necessarily come from a learner's lack of ability. It may arise because a common pace carries one unstable action into a more complex task. The key is not simply to add more practice, but to use evidence to locate the gap, correct it specifically, and then verify performance again against the original standard.",
      "diagramTitle": "From Common Pace to Mastery-Based Progression",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "Shared goal",
        "Identify the gap",
        "Targeted correction",
        "Try again",
        "Meet the standard, then progress"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "Define a clear, testable goal and standard first.",
        "Use formative evidence to identify the specific element that is not yet stable.",
        "Adjust support or practice only for the gap that has been identified.",
        "Try again under the same standard and receive feedback.",
        "Move into the more complex next task only after the standard has been met."
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "The eleven o'clock bell and the single training machine → The common timetable has a real resource rationale, but it also moves everyone to the next task at the same time.",
        "The 27.8-second, 36-gram single shot and the second check interrupted by the bell → One apparently successful attempt does not show whether the action is stable, and the fixed pace lets an unverified gap move forward.",
        "Flow starting on the same side, the lower right side of the coffee bed, and the same pattern remaining after milk steaming is removed → Formative evidence narrows the problem from 'struggling with consecutive orders' to the tamping action.",
        "The white tape, straight wrist, repositioned elbow, and the first three repetitions devoted only to levelling the coffee bed → Correction is aimed at one identified gap rather than mechanically repeating the entire routine.",
        "28.9 and 28.1 seconds, followed by 28.3 and 27.9 seconds during consecutive orders → Performance is repeatedly checked against the same morning standard, and only then does A-Lan return to latte art and the full simulation."
      ],
      "boundary": "Mastery learning is most applicable when goals can be reasonably defined, observed, and tested, and when there is some room for additional time and support. It does not mean that everyone must achieve identical outcomes, nor does it mean unlimited extensions, lower standards, or repeatedly doing the same task. In practice, targeted support can add time, material, and organizational costs. Research findings are generally positive but vary across programs, subjects, and study designs, and some self-paced settings may face completion-rate costs. The historical effect estimates reported in Bloom (1984) should not be treated as universal guarantees.",
      "reflection": "If the eleven o'clock bell had not rung, what might A-Lan's second 18-gram dose have changed?"
    },
    "moduleZh": {
      "intro": "这个模块帮助读者看见：问题不一定来自学习者能力不足，而可能来自统一进度把一个尚未稳定的具体动作带进了更复杂任务。关键不是简单增加练习次数，而是先用证据定位缺口，再针对纠正，并用原来的标准重新验证。",
      "diagramTitle": "从统一进度到达标前进",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "共同目标",
        "发现缺口",
        "针对纠正",
        "再次尝试",
        "达标前进"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "先把可检验的目标和标准说清楚。",
        "用形成性证据找出尚未稳定的具体环节。",
        "只针对已识别的缺口调整支持或练习。",
        "在相同标准下重新尝试并获得反馈。",
        "达到标准后再进入更复杂的后续任务。"
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "十一点计时铃与唯一训练机 → 统一时刻表有真实资源理由，也会把所有人同时推向下一项。",
        "27.8秒、36克的单杯与被铃声打断的第二次确认 → 一次表面合格没有暴露动作是否稳定，固定进度使未确认的缺口继续向前。",
        "同侧先出液、右侧粉面偏低以及拿掉奶泡后的重复出现 → 形成性证据把问题从“连单做不好”缩小到压粉动作。",
        "白胶带、手腕放直、肘部移正与前三次只练压平 → 纠正只针对已定位的一个缺口，而不是把整套流程机械重做。",
        "28.9、28.1以及连单中的28.3、27.9秒 → 使用上午同一标准重复验证，达标后才恢复拉花和整套模拟。"
      ],
      "boundary": "掌握学习适合目标能够被合理定义、观察和检验，并且有一定时间与支持空间的情境。它不意味着所有人都必须得到完全相同结果，也不意味着无限延时、降低标准或反复做同一任务。现实中，针对性支持会增加时间、材料与组织成本；研究结果总体积极但会随程序、学科和研究设计而变化，部分自定进度情境还可能面临完成率成本。Bloom 1984 的历史效应估计也不能当作普遍保证。",
      "reflection": "如果十一点的铃没有响，阿岚手里那第二份十八克咖啡粉可能会改变什么？"
    },
