    "fieldTitleZh": "教育科学",
    "title": "The Bookshelf That Wouldn't Make the Turn",
    "titleZh": "转不过去的书架",
    "summary": "The doorway is clearly wider than the bookshelf, yet Anning's conclusion fails at the corner. Instead of letting her keep trying at random, Teacher Zhou gives the group a way to make their movement visible and recordable, so that evidence can change what “it will fit” actually means.",
    "summaryZh": "门洞明明比书架宽，安宁的判断却在转角处失效。周老师没有让她随便试，而是给出可观察、可记录的办法，让她用证据重画“能通过”到底意味着什么。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "At four-thirty on Friday afternoon, the school’s evening book exchange was due to open at six, and the newly arrived picture books were still stacked in boxes in the corridor. The reading room needed one more bookshelf, but the main hall floor was being repaired, so the only route was through a side door. Anning measured twice with a tape: the doorway was eighty centimetres wide, while the widest part of the bookshelf was seventy-eight. Beside the scale drawing that had earned full marks the previous week, she wrote, “It will fit,” then called three classmates to help carry the shelf into the narrow corridor.",
      "The front edge went through the doorway, but the rear corner struck the doorframe while the other side touched the corridor wall. They backed out and measured again; neither number had changed. Anning spread her scale drawing on the floor. It showed the doorway and the bookshelf standing in its final position, but not the positions the shelf would pass through as it turned in from the corridor. Someone wanted to tilt it again by feel. Teacher Zhou stopped them from moving it and had them rest the shelf securely against the wall.",
      "Teacher Zhou cut a piece of stiff cardboard from one of the picture-book boxes and asked them to make a small bookshelf to scale. He then used tape on the floor to mark the corridor, doorway, and wall. He demonstrated one thing: move the cardboard a short distance, then make a pencil dot beneath one corner. After two dots, he handed the pencil to Anning. She and her classmates kept moving the model and recorded the positions of all four corners. In the space that had once been represented only by two lines for the doorframe, four curving dotted paths gradually appeared. One of them ran straight through the taped “wall.”",
      "Anning erased the original straight arrow in and out and measured again how far the shelf could move back in front of the doorway. She began with the model close to the outer side of the corridor, let the front corner clear the frame first, then backed up while turning. This time, all four corner paths stayed inside the space marked by the tape. She asked her classmates to stand at the two ends of the real bookshelf and rehearse the dotted route without carrying anything, checking that at every step they had somewhere to place their feet and enough room to change their grip. Only then did they lift the shelf again.",
      "At five forty-two, the bookshelf slowly turned into the reading room along the route marked on the floor. The front corner cleared the doorway, the rear corner drew inward, and the final side came square. Nothing touched the wall, and no one had to shout a last-minute change of direction. As soon as the shelf was steady, the classmates waiting outside opened the picture-book boxes and began filling it. Anning put the tape measure on the bottom shelf, then went back into the corridor to pick up the cardboard model from the floor.",
      "After the event, she slipped the full-mark scale drawing, the cardboard model, and a short strip of tape covered with corner dots into the assembly pouch at the bottom of the bookshelf. The red check mark was still on the front, and “78 < 80, it will fit” had not been crossed out. On the back was a new curved line made from many small dots. The final fold ran directly through the words “will fit.”"
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "周五四点半，学校晚上的换书活动六点就要开门，新到的绘本还堆在走廊纸箱里。阅览室缺一只书架，大厅又在修地板，唯一能走的是侧门。安宁拿卷尺量了两遍：门洞八十厘米，书架最宽处七十八厘米。她在上周得满分的比例图旁写下“能过”，叫上三个同学把书架抬进窄走廊。",
      "书架前沿进了门，后角却顶住门框，另一侧同时碰到走廊墙。大家退出来又量了一遍，两个数字都没变。安宁把比例图摊在地上：图里画着门洞，也画着摆正后的书架，却没有书架从走廊转进去时经过的位置。有人想凭感觉再斜一次，周老师拦住了搬动，把书架先靠墙放稳。",
      "周老师从绘本纸箱上剪下一块硬纸板，让他们按比例做一个小书架，又用胶带在地面贴出走廊、门洞和墙的位置。他先示范了一件事：纸板每移动一小段，就在一个角下面点一个铅笔点；点完两次，他把铅笔交给安宁。安宁和同伴继续移动纸板，把四个角的落点都留下。原来只画着两条门框线的地方，渐渐出现四条弯曲的点线，其中一条正穿过“墙”。",
      "安宁擦掉原先那条直进直出的箭头，重新量门前能退让的距离。她把小纸架贴近走廊外侧起步，先让前角越过门框，再边退边转；这一次，四条角点都留在胶带围出的空间里。她让同伴分别站到书架两端，先在空手状态下沿地上的点线走一遍，确认每一步都有落脚和换手的位置，才重新抬起书架。",
      "五点四十二分，书架按着地上的路线慢慢转进阅览室。前角越门、后角回收、最后一侧摆正，整个过程没有再碰墙，也没有人临时喊着改方向。书架一落稳，等在外面的同学就拆开绘本纸箱往上摆书。安宁把卷尺放到最下层，又回走廊把地上的纸板模型捡了起来。",
      "活动结束后，她把那张满分比例图、纸板模型和一小段写满角点的胶带一起塞进书架底层的装配袋。正面的红勾还在，“78＜80，能过”也没有被涂掉；背面多了一条由许多小点连成的弯线。最后一道折痕正好穿过“能过”两个字。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Constructivist learning",
    "conceptNameZh": "建构主义学习",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Constructivist learning emphasizes that learners enter new situations with existing knowledge and representations, and that when those ideas cannot explain the evidence, understanding can be reorganized through externalizing ideas, comparison, testing, and reflection. The change here is not from a “wrong number” to a “right number,” but from a static comparison of widths to an understanding of the space an object occupies while turning.",
      "The teacher does not withdraw or leave students to experiment at random. Teacher Zhou first stops the blind attempts, then provides a scale model, clear spatial boundaries, and a method for recording corner positions so that the original idea can be observed and tested. The route and explanation are still revised by the students in response to evidence. Direct instruction, demonstration, and explicit scaffolding can all be part of a constructive learning process."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "建构主义学习强调，学习者会带着已有知识和表征进入新情境，并在原有理解不能解释证据时，通过外化、比较、试验和反思重组理解。这里的变化不是从“错误数字”换成“正确数字”，而是把静态的宽度比较扩展为对物体转动过程中所占空间的理解。",
      "教师并没有退出或让学生随便试。周老师先停止盲目搬动，再提供比例模型、空间边界和记录角点的方法，使原有想法能够被观察和检验；路线和解释仍由学生依据证据修正。直接讲解、示范和明确支架都可以成为建构过程的一部分。"
    ],
