    "title": "Bag No. 27",
    "titleZh": "二十七号袋",
    "summary": "Before the submission deadline, A-Che has to make a dialogue-free closing scene readable: why does the clerk unlock the door after the shop is already closed? The expression never changes; instead, the visibility, order, and duration of the order-number shots make it easier for viewers to connect the courier with Bag No. 27, while still leaving room for different readings of the clerk’s mood.",
    "summaryZh": "交片前，阿澈必须把一场无对白的关店戏剪明白：店员为什么已经锁门，却又把门打开。同样的素材没有换表情，只通过订单号镜头的可见性、顺序和时长，就让观众更容易建立“骑手来取27号袋”的关系，同时仍保留对人物情绪的不同理解。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "On Wednesday afternoon, the film club’s short had to be submitted by six, and A-Che was still stuck on the final forty seconds. In the scene, the bakery has already closed. The clerk, Xiao Lan, locks the door, then turns back to unlock it and hands a paper bag from the counter to a courier outside. There is no dialogue and no chance to reshoot. The available footage includes a wall clock, a takeaway bag marked “27,” a shot of the courier holding a phone up to the glass with “27” clearly visible on the pickup screen, one neutral close-up of Xiao Lan, and shots of her touching the lock and handing over the bag.",
      "A-Che’s first cut was: wall clock — Xiao Lan — courier outside — unlocking the door. The paper bag did not appear until after the door had already been opened. Two classmates watched it. One thought she had decided to accept one more order; the other thought she had only just noticed someone outside. A-Che did not look for a more “obvious” facial expression. He moved the shot of Bag No. 27 to before the unlocking and placed the courier’s phone shot immediately after it.",
      "In the second cut, the “27” on the bag appeared first, but the “27” on the phone flashed by too quickly. In the screening, one person caught the match and another did not read the phone at all. A-Che held the phone shot a little longer, then cut to Xiao Lan’s close-up and her turn back toward the lock. On the next viewing, everyone could say that the person outside had come to collect the bag on the counter. But they still read Xiao Lan differently: one thought she was checking the number; another thought she already looked slightly impatient.",
      "With forty minutes left, A-Che noticed another problem. The wall clock was held so long that it pulled attention toward the question of whether she was willing to keep the shop open. He shortened it to a quick glance—just enough to establish that closing time had passed—and placed Bag No. 27 and Phone 27 closer together. Two new classmates who had not seen the earlier versions both first said, “The courier is here for Bag No. 27.” One still read Xiao Lan as impatient; the other simply thought she was checking.",
      "A-Che did not keep cutting until everyone agreed on her mood. He only checked three things: why the bag was still on the counter, why the person outside was waiting, and why the unlocking happened. Before six, he kept that version and moved the other timelines into a folder called “test cuts.” Before the final export, he trimmed two frames from the left side of the Bag No. 27 shot and watched the transition from the number, to the close-up, to the unlocking one more time.",
      "A few minutes before six, A-Che finished the export and uploaded the film to the club’s submission folder. When the progress bar reached the end, he closed the older versions in “test cuts” and left only the final timeline open."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "周三下午，电影社的短片六点必须交片，阿澈却卡在最后四十秒。戏里，面包店已经打烊，店员小岚把门锁好，转身时又回去开门，把柜台上的一个纸袋交给门外的骑手。没有对白，也不能补拍。素材里有墙钟、写着“27”的外卖袋、骑手把手机举向玻璃的一镜——取餐页上的“27”能看清——以及小岚一张平静的近景、她摸门锁和递袋的动作。",
      "阿澈的第一版是：墙钟——小岚——门外骑手——开锁，纸袋直到开门以后才出现。两个同学看完，一个以为她临时决定再接一单，另一个以为她只是刚发现门外有人。阿澈没去找更“明确”的表情；他把柜台上的27号袋拖到开锁以前，又把骑手举手机的镜头跟在后面。",
      "第二版里，纸袋上的27先出现，手机上的27却一闪而过。试看时，一个人看懂了号码对应，另一个根本没读到手机。阿澈把手机那一镜多留了一点，再接小岚近景和她回身开锁。下一次试看，几个人都能说出门外的人是来取柜台那一袋东西；但对小岚的脸，有人觉得她在确认号码，也有人觉得她已经有点不耐烦。",
      "离交片只剩四十分钟，阿澈又发现墙钟停得太久，会把注意力推向“她还要不要继续营业”。他把墙钟缩到只够交代已经关店的一眼，让27号袋和手机27靠得更近。找来的两名新同学没看过前几个版本，都先说出“骑手来取27号袋”；其中一人仍把小岚的表情读成不耐烦，另一人只觉得她在核对。",
      "阿澈没有继续剪到所有人对人物心情达成一致。他只确认了三件事：袋子为什么还在柜台上，门外的人为什么等，开锁为什么发生。六点前，他保留这一版，把其余时间线移进“试剪”文件夹。最后导出前，他把27号袋那一镜向左收了两帧，重新看了一遍号码出现、近景、开锁之间的接续。",
      "六点前几分钟，阿澈完成导出，把成片上传到电影社的交片文件夹。上传进度走完后，他关闭了“试剪”里的几个旧版本，只留下最终时间线。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Montage",
    "conceptNameZh": "蒙太奇",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Montage organizes cinematic meaning through the selection, order, duration, rhythm, and juxtaposition of shots. Adjacent shots encourage viewers to build temporal, spatial, causal, emotional, or conceptual relationships, so the same character close-up may be understood as attending to different things or acting for different reasons depending on what surrounds it.",
      "This does not guarantee that all viewers will produce exactly the same interpretation. Later research on the Kuleshov effect suggests that context can influence judgments of neutral or ambiguous facial expressions, but results vary across experiments, materials, and viewing conditions. Montage can make a particular relationship easier to infer; it cannot force every viewer into an identical psychological reading."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "蒙太奇通过镜头的选择、顺序、时长、节奏和并置来组织电影意义。相邻镜头会促使观众建立时间、空间、因果、情绪或观点上的关系，因此同一个人物近景放在不同信息之后，可能被理解为不同的注意对象或行动动机。",
      "这种作用并不保证所有观众产生完全相同的解释。关于库里肖夫效应的后续研究表明，语境可以影响对中性或含混表情的判断，但不同实验、材料与观众条件下结果并不一致。蒙太奇可以提高某种关系推断的可读性，却不能强迫所有观众得到完全相同的心理解释。"
    ],
    "mode": "concept-fable",
