    "fieldTitle": "Audio-visual techniques and media production",
    "fieldTitleZh": "视听技术与媒体制作",
    "title": "The Four Notes After the Street Corner",
    "titleZh": "街角之后的四个音",
    "summary": "Ning Jia needs the audience to hear the rehearsal behind a closed door without making the same piano phrase seem physically attached to the character after she leaves the theatre. A test listener’s “Is she wearing headphones?” forces her to rebuild the spatial continuity from rehearsal room to corridor, lobby, and street, then create a clear break before the four notes return at the end.",
    "summaryZh": "宁佳要让观众先听见门后的排练，又不让同一段钢琴在人物走出剧场后像贴在她身上一样继续。一次“她是不是戴着耳机”的试听误解，迫使她重新处理从排练室、走廊、大厅到街道的空间连续性，并为片尾重新出现的四个音留出清楚的断点。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Only one afternoon remained to mix the graduation short, and Ning Jia was stuck on a fifty-second corridor scene. The protagonist, Xiao Yu, arrives at an old theatre after work, pauses outside a closed rehearsal-room door, then decides not to go in and turns away. The final shot of the previous scene is inside that rehearsal room: someone is visibly playing a repeated four-note piano figure. The next shot cuts to Xiao Yu entering the theatre corridor. The director wants the sound to continue beyond the cut; otherwise, her pause at the door seems unmotivated.",
      "Ning Jia first carried the clear four-note phrase across the cut, then made it quieter and duller in the corridor; as Xiao Yu approached the rehearsal-room door, it became slightly clearer. The problem came in the second half. Xiao Yu left the door, crossed the lobby, and pushed open the street entrance, yet the piano remained almost equally clear. After the first screening, someone immediately asked, “Is she wearing headphones? Why does it still sound so close when she’s outside?”",
      "Ning Jia rebuilt the second half. The farther Xiao Yu moved from the rehearsal room, the more the four notes were covered by footsteps in the lobby, sounds from the ticket counter being closed down, and traffic near the street door. When the street door opened, outside sound flooded in; after the door shut behind her, the piano disappeared completely. Ning Jia kept several seconds of street image with only cars and wind. Xiao Yu continued walking, and the film did not cut back to the theatre.",
      "The director still wanted the four notes at the end because they had recurred in several earlier scenes. Ning Jia did not simply stretch the rehearsal-room track all the way into the street. She duplicated the same recording onto a separate track. Only after Xiao Yu crossed an intersection and the shot widened did the four notes return. This time, they no longer changed with her distance from the theatre, and the image did not establish any nearby on-screen source for them.",
      "At the second screening, nobody mentioned headphones. One person said that when the street door closed, the earlier piano seemed to have genuinely stayed inside the building; when it returned at the end, it felt more like the familiar music of the film coming back. Ning Jia labeled the upper track “rehearsal room” and the lower one “ending,” checked that they did not overlap by accident, then listened once more from the previous scene. When the few seconds after the street door contained only cars and wind, she pressed stop."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "毕业短片混音只剩一个下午，宁佳却卡在一段五十秒的走廊戏。女主角小榆下班后来到旧剧场，走到一扇关着的排练室门前停了一下，最后没有进去，转身离开。影片上一场的最后一镜就在排练室内：能看见有人弹琴，四个音反复出现；下一镜才切到小榆进入剧场走廊。导演希望这段声音继续到门外，否则她在门口停下会显得没来由。",
      "宁佳先让上一场清楚的四个音跨过切点，到了走廊便压低、变闷；小榆走近那扇排练室门时，声音稍微清楚一点。问题出在后半段：她离开门口，穿过大厅，再推开通向街道的大门，钢琴却仍保持着差不多的清晰度。第一次试听后，有人直接问：“她是不是戴着耳机？为什么走到街上还跟得这么近？”",
      "宁佳把后半段重新拉开。小榆离排练室越远，四个音越被大厅脚步、售票台的收拾声和街门附近的车声盖住；街门打开时，外面的声音涌进来，门在她身后合上后，钢琴彻底退掉。她保留了几秒只有车声和风的街景，小榆继续往前走，画面没有再切回剧场。",
      "导演仍想在片尾保留这四个音，因为它在前面的几场戏里已经反复出现。宁佳没有把排练室那条轨一直拖到街上，而是复制同一段录音，另开一条轨。小榆走过一个路口，镜头变成较远的街景以后，四个音才重新进入；这一遍不再随着她与剧场的距离变化，也没有和某个画内声源做空间上的呼应。",
      "第二次试听时，没人再提耳机。有人说街门一关，前面的钢琴像真的留在了楼里；片尾再出现时，则更像整部片子熟悉的那段音乐又回来了。宁佳把上面一条轨标成“排练室”，下面一条标成“片尾”，确认两者没有意外重叠。交片前，她从上一场开始最后听了一遍，等街门后的几秒只剩车声和风时，按下停止键。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Diegetic and nondiegetic sound",
    "conceptNameZh": "叙事内声与叙事外声",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Diegetic sound belongs to the story world of the film, such as character speech, environmental sound, or music with a source established within that world. Nondiegetic sound comes from outside that story-world level, such as some forms of music presented only for the audience. The key question is how the sound has been established and presented across the narrative, not what instrument produces it.",
      "Whether a sound belongs to the story world is separate from whether its source is visible on screen. Off-screen piano, footsteps, or radio can still be diegetic; whether a character can hear them also depends on distance, obstruction, scene conditions, and subjective hearing. Conversely, a lack of character reaction, unusual clarity, or an invisible source is not enough by itself to prove that a sound is nondiegetic. Earlier source establishment, spatial continuity, and the way the sound is reintroduced across the film also matter."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "叙事内声（diegetic sound）属于影片的故事世界，例如角色说话、环境声，或故事中确有声源的音乐；叙事外声（nondiegetic sound）来自故事世界之外的叙述层，例如只为观众配置的部分配乐。判断关键是声音在整段叙事中被如何建立和呈现，而不是使用了什么乐器。",
      "声音是否属于故事世界，与声源是否出现在画面里是两个维度。画外的钢琴、脚步或广播仍可以是叙事内声；角色能否听见，还取决于距离、遮挡、场景和主观听觉。反过来，不能只因为人物没有反应、声音清晰或声源不可见，就单独断定它必然是叙事外声；还要结合先前是否建立过声源、空间连续性以及影片如何重新引入这段声音。"
    ],
