    "fieldTitleZh": "时尚、室内与工业设计",
    "title": "The Green Pull Loop",
    "titleZh": "那只绿色拉环",
    "summary": "Before opening time, Xiaoran has to unfold the last display cart so her group can hang its prints. A green arrow tells her where and in which direction to act, but it does not solve the problem of a thin handle that is hard to grip. Only when the gripping method and preload are changed within the adjustable latch’s reliable locking range can she actually perform the action.",
    "summaryZh": "开放前，小然必须展开最后一辆展车才能挂上自己组的版画。绿色箭头让她知道从哪里、往哪边操作，却没有解决薄手柄难抓的问题；只有在可调搭扣保持可靠锁闭的前提下改变抓握方式和预紧，她才真正能完成这个动作。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "The community arts centre’s children’s print exhibition opened at ten, and at nine-twenty one folding display cart was still closed. Xiaoran was responsible for hanging her group’s six prints on that panel, and the works were already laid out in order on the floor. The side of the cart used an adjustable toggle latch with a threaded hook to hold the panel closed. The installer normally lifted the flat handle, which sat close to the cart body, and pulled it outward. Lu Yao had tried it himself the day before and found it easy, so he had not listed it as a setup problem.",
      "Xiaoran copied the motion she had seen the day before, but her fingertips kept slipping off the thin handle. She asked Aunt Zhou, who was steadying the cart nearby, to help. Aunt Zhou understood that the handle had to be pulled outward, but her finger joints were not well suited to pinching it from the narrow gap. Neither of them forced the panel. With less than forty minutes before opening, what worried Xiaoran most was that her six prints still had nowhere to hang.",
      "Lu Yao first made an arrow from green tape, placed it beside the handle, and wrote “pull outward.” Xiaoran immediately found the starting point and stopped trying the wrong direction, but she still could not get a secure grip. Aunt Zhou followed the arrow and still struggled to generate the initial pull. Another volunteer passing by opened it easily. Lu Yao left the arrow in place and inspected the latch itself. Its threaded hook was designed to adjust the amount of tension, and it had been tightened more than usual before transport so the panel would not rattle on the cart.",
      "He threaded a piece of wide webbing through the existing hole at the end of the handle and tied a short loop large enough for several fingers. Then he backed off the threaded hook only until the handle could still close fully and the two panels remained firmly drawn together. After every adjustment, he latched it again and shook the panel lightly to check that nothing was loose. Xiaoran could now hook her fingers through the webbing loop and pull the latch open; Aunt Zhou could also move the handle with four fingers. Lu Yao did not loosen the hook any further.",
      "At nine forty-seven, Xiaoran unfolded the panel and, with a classmate, clipped the six prints into place. The green arrow was moved to the base of the webbing loop so a first-time user could still see where to begin; the loop stayed on the latch. When they packed up after closing, Xiaoran removed the last print, folded the panel back into its transport position with her classmate, and then fastened the toggle latch shut. She pushed the panel to check that it did not move, pressed the webbing loop into the small clip on the side of the cart so it would not catch on a frame during transport, and left the green arrow in place. A little ink from the afternoon remained on one corner of the tape."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "社区艺术中心十点开儿童版画展，九点二十还剩最后一辆折叠展车没展开。小然负责把自己组的六张版画挂到那块立板上，作品已经按顺序排在地上。展车侧面用一只带螺纹挂钩的可调拉紧搭扣锁住立板；安装师傅平时掀起贴近车身的扁平手柄，再向外扳开。陆遥前一天自己试过，很顺，没把它列进布展问题。",
      "小然照着昨天见过的动作去掀，指尖却总从薄手柄上滑开。她叫正在旁边扶车的周阿姨帮忙；周阿姨知道该往外扳，手指关节却不太适合从那条窄缝里夹住手柄。两个人都停在搭扣前，没有硬掰立板。离开门不到四十分钟，小然最急的是自己的六张画还没有墙可挂。",
      "陆遥先拿绿色胶带做了一个箭头，贴在手柄旁边，又写上“向外拉”。小然马上找到起手位置，也不再试错方向，可手指依旧抓不牢；周阿姨照着箭头做，仍很难起力。路过的另一名志愿者却顺手打开了。陆遥于是留下箭头，转而检查这个搭扣本身：它的螺纹挂钩本来就用于调节拉紧程度，前一天运输前被调得偏紧，以免立板在车上晃动。",
      "他把一条宽织带穿过手柄末端原有的小孔，打成能伸进几根手指的短环；随后只回调螺纹挂钩到手柄仍能完全扣到底、两块板仍被拉紧的位置。每调一次，他都重新扣合，再抓住立板轻晃确认没有松动。小然用手指勾住织带环后能把搭扣拉开；周阿姨也能用四指带动手柄。陆遥没有再继续放松挂钩。",
      "九点四十七，小然把立板展开，和同伴把六张版画依次夹上去。绿色箭头被移到织带根部，第一次来的人仍能看出从哪里开始；织带留在搭扣上。闭馆收车时，小然先摘下最后一张版画，和同伴把立板折回运输位置，再把拉紧搭扣扣紧。她推了推板面，确认没有晃动，把织带环压进车侧的小夹片里，免得运输时勾住画框。绿色箭头还贴在拉环根部，边角沾着一点下午留下的油墨。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Affordance",
    "conceptNameZh": "可供性（Affordance）",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "In J. J. Gibson’s ecological theory of perception, an affordance is an action possibility offered by the environment relative to the capabilities of a particular actor. It is not a fixed list of functions possessed by an object in isolation, but a relation between actor and environment. The same latch can therefore offer different degrees of graspability, pullability, or operability to people with different grips, hand abilities, or bodily conditions.",
      "Don Norman later emphasized the distinction between affordances and signifiers. Arrows, labels, shapes, and other perceptible cues can indicate where to start or how to act, but the cue itself does not necessarily create a new action possibility. In the story, the green arrow improves discovery and directional understanding; the webbing loop changes the grasping condition, while the threaded hook changes the required force only within a range that still allows reliable closure. These changes expand the action for some users, but they do not imply universal suitability for every body."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "在 J. J. Gibson 的生态知觉理论中，可供性（affordance）指环境相对于某个行动者能力所提供的行动可能。它不是物体孤立拥有的一张固定功能清单，而是行动者与环境之间的关系。因此，同一个搭扣对抓握方式、手部能力或身体条件不同的人，可能提供不同程度的可抓、可拉和可操作机会。",
      "Don Norman 后来强调要区分 affordance 与 signifier（行动提示／意符）。箭头、标签、形状等线索可以告诉人“从哪里开始、往哪里操作”，但提示本身不一定创造新的行动可能。故事里，绿色箭头改善了发现和方向判断；织带拉环改变了抓握条件，而可调螺纹挂钩只在仍能可靠扣合的范围内改变所需操作力。这样的修改扩大了部分使用者能完成的动作，并不意味着对所有身体条件都普遍有效。"
    ],
