      "boundary": "Ensemble coordination does not mean that leadership disappears, nor that every ensemble should rely on distributed cues. Some situations benefit from explicit conducting, while some chamber music depends more heavily on shared prediction and real-time adaptation among members. This story shows only one coordination problem in the slowing ending of a string trio; mutual adjustment in one recording session cannot establish that one rehearsal method is best for every ensemble.",
      "reflection": "If the trio had simply learned a more accurate unified cue, why were Mo Lin and Cen Xia still able to absorb A Shen’s unplanned extra bass length during the second full take without stopping?"
