      "boundary": "“Lower is earlier” applies only to undisturbed relationships. Cuts, fills, redeposition, and missing deposits disrupt simple depth order. The four-arrow side diagram is only a simplified event chain, not a complete Harris Matrix; absolute dates also cannot be inferred without independent chronological evidence.",
      "reflection": "An apparently earlier sherd lies in the fill of a pit cutting a previously deposited layer. Which interfaces support the sequence of digging and filling, and which artifact details remain dating clues to be checked?"
