      "boundary": "Comprehensible input is not word-for-word translation and does not require reducing language to zero novelty; “i+1” is better treated as a directional idea than as an exactly calculable teaching formula. Acting correctly once from context does not automatically prove acquisition, and input is not the only sufficient condition. This story shows only that Mia is beginning to build and reuse one target form; it does not show that her use has become stable after one course. The class, characters, and events are fictional.",
