      "boundary": "Interlanguage is not a random mixture of two languages, and every fluctuation does not represent progress. Task, preparation, attention, pressure, and spoken versus written conditions often change together, so a single story cannot isolate the causal effect of each one. Feedback can also participate in learning. Multiple samples can support a cautious judgment about systematic patterns and variation at that time, but they cannot diagnose the learner’s entire language ability from one performance. The hostel, characters, and language samples are fictional.",
