    "title": "Leave the Yellow Cell Until It Is Checked",
    "summary": "The catalog locks on Friday, but the side-table carton has two heights: 78 and 82. A-Heng keeps both files in his notes while the designer continues using the earlier figure.",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "A home-goods company is updating its spring catalog, and five people need to hand dimensions, prices, and packaging information to the design team by Friday. Two weeks earlier, Xiao Cen said in a meeting that one lamp’s package height might still be old data. Manager Liang Xue was already leading the team through more than twenty fields, so everyone stopped to search the email trail. After more than ten minutes there was still no answer, and the designer was waiting to continue that page. As the meeting ended, a colleague said, “For something unverified like this, next time let’s check it first before bringing it in.” Liang Xue replied, “Right—let’s not take everyone’s time until we know.”",
      "After that, uncertain items tended to stay on individual computers until someone had checked them. By version six, A-Heng sees two outer-carton heights for the same side table: an older PDF says 78 cm and a newer email attachment says 82 cm. Remembering the earlier meeting, he saves links to both files in his personal notes and plans to update the shared sheet only after purchasing responds. Xiao Cen later sees the same 82 cm attachment and privately messages him, “Did you confirm it?” She does not flag the shared sheet either.",
      "The dimension directly affects the pallet diagram. Logistics has a net height allowance of 240 cm for the cartons themselves, with six units per layer. At 78 cm, three layers total 234 cm, so the catalog can show 18 units. At 82 cm, three layers total 246 cm, exceeding the net allowance, so only two layers and 12 units fit. Design continues using 18 units from the shared sheet, while logistics prepares a 12-unit shipping template. When the two files meet on Thursday afternoon, the pallet diagram, quantity, and related notes all need rework.",
      "Liang Xue puts both dimension files on screen and asks when A-Heng saw the new attachment. Tuesday, he says; Xiao Cen says she saw it too. Liang Xue closes the rework list. “Last time I told you not to take everyone’s time. We’ve gone the long way around. Put both sources up, even before we have the answer.” A-Heng adds a yellow pending-verification cell beside 78, assigning Purchasing and 14:00. The designer moves to other pages rather than asking him to take the question away until it is resolved.",
      "Xiao Cen adds the new email link to the yellow cell and asks Purchasing which packing sheet it needs. This time, her question remains where everyone can see it. At 13:30, Purchasing obtains the supplier’s formal document and confirms 82 cm. A-Heng updates the height. Another colleague checks the model and original document before clearing yellow. Design changes three layers and 18 units to two layers and 12; Logistics updates its template to match.",
      "Before the catalog is locked on Friday, the source sheet contains only white, verified fields. When the printer produces the proof, the side-table entry reads “12 units per pallet.” The supplier packing-sheet link remains beside the 82 cm field, and the reviewer’s name appears in the final column."
    ],
    "overall": "Psychological safety is the shared expectation within a team about the interpersonal consequences of asking questions, admitting uncertainty, or raising disagreement. That expectation can affect whether concerns enter shared work early, while still coexisting with verification and high standards.",
    "conceptName": "Psychological safety",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "No one is humiliated, but the accepted precedent that unverified questions consume everyone’s time makes the social cost visible. Both A-Heng and Xiao Cen later keep the same 78/82 discrepancy in private channels until rework appears.",
      "The later response allows unresolved issues to be exposed early while preserving sources, ownership, deadlines, and a second-person check. Psychological safety changes expectations around speaking up; it does not turn unverified data into final answers."
    ],
    "module": {
      "intro": "Observe the team’s shared expectation about what will happen when someone raises an early uncertainty, and whether that expectation changes when information enters shared work.",
      "diagramTitle": "How 78/82 cm Moves from Private Notes into the Shared Sheet",
      "diagramSteps": [
        "Create a speaking-up precedent that the team collectively notices",
        "Have multiple members keep a new concern in private channels",
        "Let different functions continue with different numbers and incur rework",
        "Change the manager’s response to early uncertainty",
        "Publish the same dimension conflict while still requiring source confirmation and review"
      ],
      "diagramStepNotes": [
        "Liang Xue endorses “check it first,” creating a perceivable social cost for bringing unverified concerns.",
        "A-Heng keeps the 78/82 cm conflict in personal notes, while Xiao Cen uses only a private message.",
        "With 240 cm of net carton height, 78×3 = 234 allows 18 units; 82×3 = 246 exceeds the limit, so only two layers and 12 units fit.",
        "The manager explicitly permits pending-verification flags while still requiring sources, an owner, and a deadline.",
        "At 13:30, Purchasing confirms 82 cm from the formal packing sheet; another person checks the model and source before clearing yellow."
      ],
      "mapping": [
        "Personal notes and private messages → key uncertainty remains outside shared visibility.",
        "240 cm net carton height → directly checkable basis for the 18-versus-12-unit difference.",
        "Yellow pending-verification cell → permission to expose information that is not yet final.",
        "Packing sheet + reviewer → evidence and responsibility remain after speaking up."
      ],
      "boundary": "Psychological safety is not the claim that every idea is correct, nor is it the same as general friendliness or a manager simply saying “please speak up.” The rework in this story establishes only this local behavior chain; professional standards, evidence, and task accountability remain separate requirements.",
      "reflection": "If several team members keep the same kind of uncertainty in private channels, what response would help it enter shared work earlier without allowing unverified data to flow directly into final output?"
    },
