    "collection": "field-core-fables",
    "storyBody": "The blue-lamp workshop had seven nights to make sixty wick crystals for the harbour. Its rule was carved above the furnace: two measures of green powder combine with one measure of silver powder to make one crystal. Apprentice Luo remembered only that silver supplied the brilliant colour. When the first firing looked pale, he doubled the silver in every bowl. The furnace produced no extra crystals. A costly metallic paste remained at the bottom, and the harbour clerk had already counted the promised lamps.\n\nLuo hid the residue under fresh powder until the master's scale exposed the added weight. The master did not lecture him. She placed ten green counters and ten silver counters on the bench, then grouped two green with one silver. Five complete groups appeared; five silver counters remained alone. With ten usable measures of green and ten of silver, green was exhausted first and limited the batch to five crystals. Another measure of silver could not stand in for the missing pair of green.\n\nThe workshop ordered more green powder at emergency price. Yet the next firing yielded only four crystals from material planned for five. Luo blamed the ratio until he washed a sample and found pale sand in the sack. The supplier's mark said eighty percent pure. Ten weighed measures therefore contained only eight usable green measures, enough for four groups with four silver measures. To obtain ten usable measures, they would need twelve and a half measured units of that impure stock, assuming the purity claim was itself sound.\n\nTwo nights remained. Luo set the adulterated sack on the master's desk and reported it, though the harbour deadline would now be missed. Past ledgers showed that firing and handling usually recovered nine of every ten predicted crystals; side products and fragments took the rest. Sixty delivered lamps therefore required more than sixty as a theoretical target. Quietly adding powder and hoping every predicted crystal survived would hide both purity and yield. The recipe fixed conserved ratios, while purity set usable input and the process set actual yield. None of those numbers said how quickly the furnace would run.\n\nThe master refused to seal weak crystals into lamp housings. She returned the sack, bought clean green powder, and cancelled the workshop's decorative window order to pay the surcharge. Luo weighed 132 green measures and 66 silver measures for a theoretical sixty-six crystals. At their usual ninety-percent recovery they expected about fifty-nine, so they prepared one additional correctly proportioned bowl rather than pouring in silver blindly. The arithmetic did not guarantee the outcome, but it made the risk visible before the furnace door closed.\n\nA cracked shelf spoiled two crystals on the sixth night. The master sent word that the last lamps would arrive after the first tide and accepted the harbour's late fee. Luo wanted to add a final scoop of silver to 'make up' the loss. She pointed instead to the intact leftover bowl: two green, one silver. They fired that group, inspected the wick, and delivered the missing lamp at noon.\n\nWhen the accounts were settled, the late fee and clean powder consumed the workshop's festival bonus. Luo scraped the earlier silver paste from the cold furnace and returned it to a labelled recovery jar. At the next mixing, he set down two green scoops, then one silver. The second silver jar remained closed, its lid still bearing the blue thumbprint from his first mistake.",
    "storyBodyZh": "蓝灯坊要在七夜内为港口做出六十枚灯芯晶。炉口刻着配方：两份青粉与一份银粉合成一枚晶体。学徒阿洛只记得银粉带来亮蓝色，第一炉颜色偏淡时，他便把每碗银粉加倍。晶体没有多一枚，炉底却积下一层昂贵银泥；港口书吏已经按六十盏登记了船位。\n\n阿洛用新粉盖住残渣，还是被师傅从炉重里查出。师傅没有讲大道理，只在桌上摆十枚青筹和十枚银筹，每两青配一银。最后只有五个完整小组，另有五枚银筹孤零零剩着。十份青粉与十份银粉最多做五枚晶体，因为青粉先耗尽；再添银粉，也补不出缺少的两份青粉。\n\n灯坊高价买来新青粉，下一炉却只得到四枚，原本按五枚配的料少了一枚。阿洛怀疑比例，洗过样品后才发现袋里混着浅色砂粒。供货标记写着纯度八成：称十份，只含八份可用青粉，恰好能配四份银粉、做四组。要得到十份纯料，需称十二点五份这样的存货，还得先相信那枚八成印章。\n\n只剩两夜。阿洛把杂料袋放到师傅桌上，如实报告，港口期限也因此注定赶不上。旧账显示，每十枚理论晶体通常只能收回九枚，裂片、旁生成分和搬运会吃掉余数。交付六十枚，就不能只准备六十枚理论量；悄悄多倒几勺、赌每枚都成形，只会把纯度与收率一同藏掉。配方决定守恒比例，纯度决定可用原料，工序决定实际收率；这些都不等于炉火需要的时间。\n\n师傅拒绝把脆弱晶体封进灯壳。她退掉杂料，买下干净青粉，又取消自家橱窗装饰来填差价。两人先配一百三十二份青粉和六十六份银粉，理论上可得六十六枚；按九成收率约为五十九枚，于是再准备一碗比例正确的材料，而不是盲目添银。数字不能保证成品，却在关炉前把风险摆到了桌面。\n\n第六夜，一块开裂炉板又毁掉两枚。师傅通知港口最后几盏要错过首班潮水，接受误期罚金。阿洛伸手去拿银勺，想把损失“补回来”。师傅指向剩下那碗完整配料：两青、一银。他们烧完这一组，检查灯芯，正午送出了最后一盏。\n\n结账时，迟交罚金和净料差价吃掉了全坊的节庆奖金。阿洛从冷炉里刮出早先的银泥，装进写明“回收”的罐。下一次配料，他放下两勺青粉，再取一勺银粉。第二只银罐始终没有打开，盖上还留着他第一次多加时按下的蓝色指印。",
    "explanation": "Stoichiometry uses balanced equations and conservation to relate quantities of reactants and products through particle or mole ratios. The limiting reactant determines theoretical yield, while other materials may remain in excess. Real materials require molar mass, concentration, purity, and units, and incomplete reaction, impurities, or loss reduce actual yield.",
    "explanationZh": "化学计量依据配平方程与守恒关系，把反应物和产物数量按粒子或摩尔比联系起来。限制反应物决定理论产率，其他材料可能过量。处理实物还需考虑摩尔质量、浓度、纯度和单位；不完全反应、杂质与损失会使实际产率更低。"
