    "explanation": "Plate tectonics describes the lithosphere as relatively moving plates whose divergent, convergent, and transform boundaries organise earthquakes, volcanoes, mountain building, and ocean-basin change. Oceanic lithosphere forms at spreading ridges and is recycled at subduction zones. The framework identifies hazard patterns but cannot provide exact earthquake timing.",
