    "explanation": "Residence time describes how long material spends inside a piece of equipment or system. Volume divided by flow gives only a nominal average. Real fluid has a distribution: short-circuiting lets some material leave too early, while dead zones hold some too long. Tracer tests, mixing patterns, and equipment geometry can reveal and improve that distribution, which often determines reaction or treatment performance.",
    "explanationZh": "停留时间描述物料在设备或系统内经历多久。体积除以流量只给出名义平均值，真实流体可能形成停留时间分布：短路流使部分物料过早离开，死区则让部分物料滞留过久。示踪实验、混合方式和设备几何可帮助识别并改善这种差异，而反应或处理效果往往取决于整条分布。"
