    "explanation": "Differential diagnosis is a structured process of generating plausible explanations, prioritizing them by likelihood and the harm of missing them, seeking evidence that distinguishes among them, and updating the list as findings change. It avoids both premature closure on the first fitting answer and indiscriminate pursuit of every rare condition. Clinicians combine history, examination, appropriate tests, reassessment, and safety-netting; more than one cause may coexist. The story is fictional and illustrates reasoning rather than a diagnostic checklist. Real symptoms require individualized professional assessment, especially when they are severe, new, or worsening.",
    "explanationZh": "鉴别诊断是提出合理候选、按可能性与漏诊危害排序，再用能区分候选的证据不断更新判断的过程。它既防止过早停在第一个顺眼答案，也避免无差别追查所有罕见病。临床上需结合病史、检查、适当检验、复评与安全网，并容许多种原因并存。故事仅示范推理，不是症状清单；真实不适应由专业人员个体评估。"
