    "explanation": "Drug interactions occur when a medicine, food, or other substance changes another medicine's exposure through absorption, metabolism, transport, or excretion, or changes its effect through additive, opposing, or other pharmacodynamic mechanisms. Clinical importance depends on substance, dose, timing, person, purpose, and evidence. Complete medication reconciliation and professional judgement are more reliable than isolated lists or self-directed timing changes.",
    "explanationZh": "药物相互作用是药物、食物或其他物质通过改变吸收、代谢、转运、排泄等药代过程，或通过叠加、拮抗等药效过程，改变另一种药的暴露或作用。临床重要性取决于物质、剂量、时机、个体、用途与证据。完整用药核对和专业判断比孤立清单或自行错时服用更可靠。"
