    "explanation": "Herb-drug interactions occur when a herbal product changes medicine exposure or effects through absorption, metabolism, transport, excretion, or physiological action. Product identity, quality, concentration, dose, timing, individual factors, and the medicine's therapeutic window affect risk. Evidence for many proposed interactions remains limited, so neither assuming natural means safe nor stopping medicines from a generic list is appropriate; complete reconciliation and professional assessment are more reliable.",
