    "explanation": "Standardisation and personalisation in service require deliberate boundaries between reliable common processes and individual goals, needs, contexts, and preferences. Steps needed for safety, quality, and continuity remain stable; elements related to fit and dignity can vary with authorization, resources, and records for handover. Personalization is not absence of rules, while standardization should not flatten every user into one person.",
    "explanationZh": "服务标准化与个性化是在可靠共同流程和个体目标、需要、情境与偏好之间设计边界。安全、质量和连续所需步骤应稳定，适配与尊严相关部分可在授权和资源支持下变化，并留下记录供交接。个性化不是无规则，标准化也不应把所有使用者压成同一种人。"
